# roam-277: chrome://flags/#roamux-new-tab-position — the kill-switch for
# kNewTabPosition (patch 0068's seam + patch 0070's Settings row). Structural
# precedent: patches 0064 (roam-266) and 0066 (roam-269).
#
# Lands in the SAME change as the feature: since roam-226 every Roamux flag
# ships default-ON with an opt-out entry, and without this row this would be
# the only default-on Roamux feature a user cannot turn off.
#
# THREE files, matching 0064/0066 exactly: (1) chrome/browser/about_flags.cc —
# one FeatureEntry, kOsMac, name and description INLINED (no roamux-owned
# flag-descriptions unit; anchored directly after 0066's entry — ORDERING
# DEPENDENCY: stays AFTER 0066 in name order); (2) chrome/browser/flag-metadata.json
# — the row in GLOBAL ALPHABETICAL ORDER (between roamux-initial-url and
# roamux-refresh-all-initial-urls), owner set, expiry_milestone -1;
# (3) chrome/browser/flag-never-expire-list.json — REQUIRED by expiry -1.
#
# CI-INVISIBLE GATE: AboutFlagsTest lives in `unit_tests`, which no Roamux CI
# job builds; it enforces the alphabetical order and `expiry -1 subset-of
# never-expire-list`. Run it locally on any change to these three files
# (DYLD_FRAMEWORK_PATH for Sparkle) — done for this patch.
#
# Flag-off behaviour: chrome::NewTab() never reads the pref and runs the
# stock patch-0067 request (end of the active tab's group); the Settings
# "New tab position" row is not stamped. Nothing is stranded.
diff --git a/chrome/browser/about_flags.cc b/chrome/browser/about_flags.cc
index e111777e39..c1b41761de 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/about_flags.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/about_flags.cc
@@ -4768,6 +4768,18 @@ const FeatureEntry kFeatureEntries[] = {
      "remove the shortcut and the tab-menu item.",
      kOsMac,
      FEATURE_VALUE_TYPE(roamux::features::kRefreshAllInitialUrls)},
+    // Roamux (roam-277): where Cmd+T / "+" / File > New Tab insert the new
+    // tab (Settings > Appearance > "New tab position"). Ships default-on like
+    // every Roamux flag since roam-226, so this entry IS the kill-switch and
+    // lands in the same change as the feature (the roam-266/269 precedent).
+    // Turning it off restores the stock patch-0067 behaviour (end of the
+    // active tab's group) and hides the Settings row; the pref is never read.
+    {"roamux-new-tab-position", "Roamux: new tab position",
+     "Adds a Settings > Appearance option that decides where a new tab "
+     "(Cmd+T, the + button, File > New Tab) is inserted: at the end of the "
+     "tab strip, at the end of the current tab's group, or right after the "
+     "current tab. Turn this off to remove the setting and use the default.",
+     kOsMac, FEATURE_VALUE_TYPE(roamux::features::kNewTabPosition)},
     // Roamux (roam-31): developer mirror of
     // roamux.signin.optional_entry_point_enabled (E5). Functional sign-in
     // additionally requires a keyed-and-authorized build (three-state
